<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<subsection xml:id="sec-ferpa">
  <title>FERPA</title>

  <p>
    Once you enter college, regardless of age (including minors), you have the right to privacy.
    Midland College employees cannot discuss your grades, or any aspect of your performance, work habits,
    attendance, participation, or anything else with anyone who does not have an academic
    need to know (an example of a person with an academic need to know is an advisor who is working
    with you to register for the next semester).
  </p>

  <p>
    If you wish for your instructor to discuss any aspect of a class that pertains specifically to you, with anyone, you
    will need to complete a FERPA waiver through the portal.  This waiver details what your instructor is allowed to discuss
    with whom.
  </p>

  <p>
    Please note: It is my policy that I will not participate in any discussion until I have
    verified with the registrar and records office that the FERPA waiver is complete and active. I
    also will not participate in the discussion without you taking an active role in the conversation.
  </p>

  <p>
    To complete a FERPA Waiver:
    <ol>
      <li>Sign into the portal.</li>
      <li>Click on the <em>Students</em> tab.</li>
      <li>Click on <em>Transcripts and Forms</em>.</li>
      <li>Click on <em>FERPA Permissions</em> (bottom of the page).</li>
      <li>Fill out and submit the electronic form.</li>
    </ol>
  </p>
</subsection>
